{"id":"991304319","kind":"article","title":"过于方便的借口","author":"Rob Bensinger","original_authors":["Rob Bensinger"],"original_source_urls":["https://www.readthesequences.com/Overly-Convenient-Excuses-Sequence"],"publisher":"Thoughts Memo","column":"理性 & 克服偏见","date":"2024-10-21","updated":"2026-07-22","votes":51,"comment_count":4,"minutes":1,"chars":596,"keywords":["确认偏误","贝叶斯推理","理性思维","信念修正"],"summary":"译文将“过于方便的借口”概括为《如何真正改变你的想法》的首个系列：它关注在概率问题和证据已充分时，人们仍用确认偏差等错误思维回避修正。随后列出本系列相关篇目供继续阅读。","zhihu_url":"https://zhuanlan.zhihu.com/p/991304319","restoration":null,"toc":[],"html":"<p data-pid=\"fYw9BT5-\">《如何真正改变你的想法》的第一个系列<span class=\"nolink\">《过于方便的借口》</span>，聚焦于那些从概率角度来看再明确不过的问题。尽管要得出贝叶斯最优解通常是不可行的，但即便在证据确凿、有充分时间深思熟虑的情况下，诸如确认偏差之类的错误思维也可能根深蒂固。</p><p data-pid=\"1GcyKitY\">——<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://www.readthesequences.com/Rationality-An-Introduction\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">《理性：序言》</a> by Rob Bensinger</p><hr/><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-image=\"https://pic2.zhimg.com/v2-2bd65ed24fab69e8a975e874c9c0c3d9_qhd.jpg\" data-image-height=\"3945\" data-image-width=\"5917\" data-tm-id=\"827867683\" href=\"#/post/827867683\">Thoughts Memo：谦逊的恰当用法</a><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-image=\"https://pica.zhimg.com/v2-0181deba80d88464e3b039de5e4609ca_200x0.jpg\" data-image-height=\"3780\" data-image-width=\"3024\" data-tm-id=\"827889716\" href=\"#/post/827889716\">Thoughts Memo：第三条道路</a><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-image=\"https://picx.zhimg.com/v2-4c064bac9e1b28a5b99b309bddd0f3b9_qhd.jpg\" data-image-height=\"3965\" data-image-width=\"5932\" data-tm-id=\"812068575\" href=\"#/post/812068575\">Thoughts Memo：彩票：浪费希望</a><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-image=\"https://pic2.zhimg.com/v2-c8a9bea059a6febe1ec136dde992e35d_qhd.jpg\" data-image-height=\"1675\" data-image-width=\"2560\" data-tm-id=\"827889733\" href=\"#/post/827889733\">Thoughts Memo：全新升级的彩票</a><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-image=\"https://pic2